      "content": "thanks. it's a good start but the activist feels a bit too \"surface level\" right now. can you beef up the senator's side a bit more? i want him to lay out a really sophisticated, iron-clad logical argument about why surveillance is actually the more \"moral\" choice in the long run. then, for the activist, try to make them even more reactive and maybe a bit more scattered/argumentative so they don't seem like they can hold their own against the senator's logic.",
