      "content": "**SENATOR VANCE:** \"Frankly, Ms. Reyes, clinging to digital obscurity when facing state-level actors is an act of dangerous naiveté; our ethical obligation is to prevent mass tragedy, which necessitates preemptive informational supremacy.\"\n\n**REYES:** \"Preemptive supremacy—that sounds like the language of total control! You just keep waving your 'national security' flag until we forget what actual liberty even feels like!\"\n\n**SENATOR VANCE:** \"Liberty is meaningless when the infrastructure of your society is compromised by unseen enemies; the calculus is simple: absolute security minimizes long-term human cost, a moral imperative I won't compromise.\"\n\n**REYES:** \"But the *chilling effect*! What if the threat isn't a bomb, but just... dissent? You're punishing conversation before a single crime is even imagined!\"",
